{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1302135-shifters-in-the-dreaming","id":1302135,"title":"Shifters in The Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-03T00:36:51-07:00","id":1302135,"title":"Shifters in The Dreaming","content":"I've just started in a mixed game, and I'm having trouble finding crossover information for mixing 'spirit' worlds. I'm playing a changeling in a game with mostly other changelings and shifters. We're not going exceedingly strict with rules, but I like to keep a general framework in mind. However, shifter spirit stuff/Umbra is probably my weakest WoD area.<br /> <br /> Without getting into IC details, my changeling unexpectedly ended up pulled into the Umbra with a group. On the spot, I assumed his mien would be visible to everyone and that they'd forget once they were out of the Umbra. If anyone has extra thoughts regarding changelings in the Umbra, I'm all ears.<br /> <br /> I want to be prepared for the possibility of shifters in the Dreaming. IC, we're running into an issue of some shifters utterly dismissing any changeling-related pressures. We have a common antagonist, but the IC respect for the changeling needs is a growing problem. I'm musing with the idea of shocking them with a glimpse of the Dreaming.<br /> <br /> If I go that route:<br /> 1. Would a shifter need to be Enchanted independently before being able to enter The Dreaming?<br /> 2. Would a shifter be able to physically enter and exit The Dreaming through a Trod in something like a freehold as a changeling would?<br /> 3. Assuming it's not a super Banal shifter like an Ananasi, would The Dreaming or Chimera react any differently to them than to a changeling?<br /> 4. Would there be an expression of their shifter nature in the way a fae mien dominates a changeling's appearance?<br /> 5. Would umbral spirits react or care at all?<br /> <br /> Thanks for your input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25169-obieblu","user":"obieblu","date":". 04-03-2019, 04:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25169-obieblu","name":"obieblu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T02:53:21-07:00","id":1302147,"title":"","content":"1. Yes and no. Personally I would say that merely entering Dreaming Enchants them though that is not directly stated. Reading through Dreams and Nightmares implies that one can enter un-enchanted but the Chimerical is still obvious and real for any who enter. If one ventures into the Far Dreaming then the Silver Paths and Trods within cannot hold the weight of the un-enchanted but being specifically enchanted will allow them to travel on both for the duration of the enchantment. On the other hand it is explicitly said that no one can enter the Deep Dreaming without being enchanted, if some magic (mostly of the Awakened kind) succeeds in going around this restriction that person will loose all recollection of the waking world unless enchanted by a Changeling.<br /> <br /> There is a mention in the Near Dreaming part about mortals needing to be Enchanted to enter the Dreaming physically so that would imply that one would need to be enchanted to enter but why then the mentions of how the un-enchanted are affected in the Far Dreaming? So like I said personally I would say that one needs to be enchanted within the Dreaming or one will be rejected one way or another, but that is just my personal opinion.<br /> <br /> Also remember that eating food in the Dreaming, especially in the deeper regions, will enchant the eater and especially so in the Deep Dreaming where the eater will also be fairy stroked loosing all sense of self.<br /> <br /> 2. There are Paths of Balor, Green ones perhaps my memory is a bit hazy, that run between Dreaming and the Umbrae and through those the Garou could enter perhaps even on their own, but the Paths of Balor are often one way streets so they would need to find a new way out. A Changeling could on the other hand help a Garou through a freehold into the Dreaming proper.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes. They are still not native to the Dreaming and thus are under it\u2019s scrutinity and the Chimera are likely to be more wary or even hostile to prodigals in the Dreaming depending on the chimeras own nature. But they will not likely be treated quite like the Kithain for whom this is their native land.<br /> <br /> 4. I dont recall there being any ruling on this but personally I would say that their nature, and especially their rage, can be expressed on their persons or in the immediate surroundings with the extremety of expression depending upon how Deep within the Dreaming you are. Near they might have a wild look on them and their clothes, in the Far some expressions of their specific animal nature might come to fore along with their rage manifesting in looking menacing Etc. And in the Deep their animal nature should be clearly identifiable, even if they are in homid, with those bearing rage, especially high values, having the environment itself reacting to it by sharpening Shadows, cracking the earth beneath their feet with hissing fissures Etc.<br /> <br /> But that is only how I would likely play it so YMMV.<br /> <br /> 5. React to what? Changelings in the Umbra? Or being shunted in the Dreaming? Probably yes to both but in different ways. Changelings, Kithain particularly, in the Umbra are rare visitors and so may cause some waryness or even aggression depending upon the spirit. Weaver spirits would be aggressive most likely while Wyld spirits would be either indifferent or happy to see them depending on their current mood and Wyrm spirits likely react aggressively especially if the Fae are with Garou. Nunnehi on the other hand would not raise many eyebrows at all amongst the spirits and they would act in no particularly special manner. Being shunted into the Dreaming would likely be a cause of concern for any spirit though, especially weaver spirit who would likely get the wrong sort of attention from the Dreaming itself.<br /> <br /> Dreams and Nightmares is the book to look for in any of these matters though if you want to see for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:08:09-07:00","id":1302180,"title":"","content":"In re 2, there're three types of Paths of Balor, one for each of the Umbrae (Gold for High, Green for Middle, Black for Low). The relevant type for shifters are the Green Paths of Balor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T22:48:39-07:00","id":1302474,"title":"","content":"Thank you, especially <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1629_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1629\" data-vbnamecard=\"1629\">Possessed</a> for such a detailed answer.<br /> <br /> I have Dreams &amp; Nightmares in a box in my mother's attic on the other side of the world. I didn't remember if it had a lot of specific info for Prodigals in the Dreaming. I remembered the Deep Dreaming may attack changelings for their sliver of Banality. I thought it plausible it could react differently to other critters. I always held the impression that someone gets Enchanted on-the-way through to the Dreaming, or they wouldn't be there, not being able to see/interact with anything if they weren't. I should have clarified about umbral spirits reacting. I was thinking about their totems any spirit companions going &quot;WTF did you go?&quot; if they couldn't see/sense them or following them into the Dreaming and if that would mean anything. It's probably not terribly important, but it crossed my mind.<br /> <br /> These answers are good enough for what I need. Thank you!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25169-obieblu","name":"obieblu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-05T10:45:24-07:00","id":1302862,"title":"","content":"We played it as changeling feeling like two people while in the Umbra. Since weaver spawn are essentially Banal, Kithain (and kinain with Kenning) can sense their presence whether or not they're visible or even present yet. Any Prodigal that ends up in the Dreaming self-enchants once they breath in air. They may be disoriented for awhile, but they'll be fine once they adjust.<br /> <br /> Prodigals and humans can get by on a single sip of water and a single cookie -- or a similarly-sized foodstuff -- per day. The problem is that food and water tastes really good in the Dreaming. And you want more of it. Garou and Shifters are immune to Bedlam and becoming Dreamstruck because of their half-spirit natures. Humans, however, are not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1973-saint-michael","name":"Saint Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1973_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}